# Responsive Dimensions Rules

- Never use hardcoded UI sizing for layout, text, or icons (for example `fontSize: 14`, `width: 100`).
- For horizontal layout spacing/sizing, use `widthScale(...)`.
- For vertical spacing/sizing, use `heightScale(...)`.
- For softer component sizing (buttons/cards/radius/padding), use `moderateWidthScale(...)` or `moderateHeightScale(...)`.
- For typography, always use `fontScale(...)` or `fontSize.size*` from `src/config/fonts.ts`.
- For icon sizes, always use `iconScale(...)`.
- For tablet/TV behavior, use `responsiveMetrics` flags (`isTablet`, `isLargeTablet`, `isTV`) instead of device-specific magic numbers.

## Example

```tsx
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  title: { fontSize: fontScale(16) },
  card: { padding: moderateWidthScale(12), borderRadius: moderateWidthScale(10) },
});
```
